       }
      ],
      "text": "HFrEF:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " now second-line, for patients who can't take an ARNI (intolerance, unavailable, cost). Stop the ACE inhibitor 36 hours before starting sacubitril/valsartan."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Lisinopril for HF:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " start 5 mg once daily, increase as tolerated to 40 mg daily."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Check electrolytes and renal function before starting, at 1 month, and after each significant dose increase or clinical change; reduce or hold the dose during dehydration or acute renal decline."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Lisinopril:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " K-sparing diuretics raise hyperkalemia risk; NSAIDs raise renal-impairment risk and blunt the BP effect; lithium toxicity has been reported (monitor lithium levels); contraindicated with a neprilysin inhibitor (sacubitril); no aliskiren in diabetes."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Lisinopril overdose:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " hypotension is most likely, treated with IV normal saline; lisinopril can be removed by hemodialysis."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
